#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# precision

#% text
# `precision(x)` gives the number of correct significant decimal digits of `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact numbers have precision `inf`; machine reals 15.95 (their 53 bits); a ball the digits its radius leaves correct. For an expression it is the least precision of its numbers.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
precision(1/3)
#% output
#= inf

#% cell
precision(0.5)
#% output
#= 15.954589770191003

#% cell
precision(n(pi, 30))
#% output
#= 34.91947949702182

#% cell
precision(1~20)
#% output
#= 20.16900970948674

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The least precision of an expression:

#% cell
precision(1~30 + x*2~10)
#% output
#= 10.23501985257536

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Arithmetic with balls tracks the error, so precision is lost on cancellation:

#% cell
a = n(1 + 10^-15, 25); precision(a - 1)
#% output
#= 15.006089553390062

#% text
# `set_precision` sets it:

#% cell
precision(set_precision(0.1, 40))
#% output
#= 40.0369894233095

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `accuracy`, `set_precision`, `n`
